{"name":"Beeswax","hex":"#e9d7ab","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beeswax","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A wax secreted by bees from which they make honeycomb; or, the processed form of this wax used in the manufacture of various goods.","Business."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To polish with beeswax."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beeswax"}],"entries":[{"title":"Beeswax","blocks":[{"text":"Beeswax is a natural wax produced by honey bees of the genus Apis. The wax is formed into scales by eight wax-producing glands in the abdominal segments of worker bees, which discard it in or at the hive. The hive workers collect and use it to form cells for honey storage and larval and pupal protection within the beehive. Chemically, beeswax consists mainly of esters of fatty acids and various long-chain alcohols."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Honey_comb.jpg/330px-Honey_comb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beeswax"},{"title":"Beeswax (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Beeswax is a 2009 American mumblecore film written and directed by Andrew Bujalski. The film examines a few days in the life of twins, played by real-life sisters Tilly and Maggie Hatcher."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/de/Beeswax_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beeswax_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Beeswax.jpg/500px-Beeswax.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Beeswax.jpg/1280px-Beeswax.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Beeswax.jpg/500px-Beeswax.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip